cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these data, please cite the paper and this archived version."
title: "BaySimChip: R Shiny app and analysis code for 'Quantitative modeling of platform-specific processes to improve pharmacokinetic studies in organ-on-a-chip systems'"
version: 1.0.0
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amiri
    given-names: Behnam
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6824-2741"
    affiliation: "Bayer AG, Berlin, Germany (present address: ESQlabs GmbH)"
  - family-names: Vural
    given-names: Özlem
    affiliation: "Bayer AG, Berlin, Germany"
  - family-names: Raschke
    given-names: Marian
    affiliation: "Bayer AG, Berlin, Germany"
  - family-names: Steger-Hartmann
    given-names: Thomas
    affiliation: "Bayer AG, Berlin, Germany"
  - family-names: Reichel
    given-names: Andreas
    affiliation: "Bayer AG, Berlin, Germany"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  BaySimChip is an R Shiny app for compartmental pharmacokinetic models of
  organ-on-a-chip systems: build the model of a chip, define the experimental
  conditions (dosing, sampling, media exchange, evaporation, non-specific
  binding), simulate concentration-time profiles and estimate parameters such
  as intrinsic clearance and permeability from measured data. The repository
  also contains the R code, the processed concentration-time data and the
  results that reproduce the analyses and figures of the paper.
keywords:
  - organ-on-a-chip
  - microphysiological systems
  - pharmacokinetics
  - compartmental modelling
  - evaporation
  - sampling
  - non-specific binding
  - parameter estimation
  - R Shiny
